> [Trump]’s executive order on religious freedom allows HHS Secretary Tom Price to cut access to affordable contraceptive services from their health insurance plans.
The subject line of the press release from HHS Secretary Tom Price in response to President Trump�[�]s signing of the Religious[ Liberty] executive order[ said] it all[,] �[�]Secretary Price Welcomes Opportunity to Reexamine Cont[race]ption Mandate�[�]. The executive order frees Price to take aim at covered women�[�s] health services that providers, insurers[,] and employers may find objectionable under their religious beliefs. Price has an antiquated and paternalistic perspective that men should be in charge of the[ type of] health care services[ a] woman have access to.
